    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A seasonal opening of routes along the frontier zone saw crossings surge, with data trackers noting a numerical change from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. This movement along the U.S. border, driven by favorable travel conditions, contrasts with year-to-date immigration statistics that remain near multi-decade lows, a border security effect of asylum shutdown and deportation policies. The path forward is constrained by political gridlock as legislators remain deadlocked over funding for enforcement agencies.",
