    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The spring weather brought a climatic change, opening new pathways for boundary crossers to move along the geopolitical line. A statistical trend emerged as apprehensions increased, a key border activity metric along this international boundary. Yet, the frontier remains guarded, with crossings restricted by policy measures that keep immigration statistics at historic lows. This tension between the urge to explore new routes and the enforcement policy outcome highlights a complex journey at the border area.",
